<h2>Classification and validation</h2>
<p>This is operational scheduling, not a browser plug, protocol, or intent. Sampling, admission, atomic reservation and execution remain separate. The <a href="/docs/agent/platform-decisions.md#heavy-command-admission-queue">standing admission rule</a> supports conservative capacity bounds and reserved workstation headroom; it does not itself settle adaptive ownership. Keeping the operator envelope independent of future adaptive strategies is this proposed extension. Related open work #6678 supplies weighted-accounting requirements, not a ratified premise.</p>
<p>A promotion comparison needs joined command kind, policy version, wait, occupancy, resource signals, duration and outcome. Report excluded records, wait tails, throughput, timeouts and pressure together. Add tests for simultaneous expansion, oversized proposals, stale/partial input, natural drain and deferred fallback before a future controller is enabled.</p>
